<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Agent Perimeter — MCP ecosystem census</title>
<style>{{ css|safe }}</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>MCP ecosystem census</h1>
<p class="mono">registry endpoint: {{ run.registry_endpoint }}</p>

<h2>Headline</h2>
<div class="strip">
<p data-testid="unknown-count"><strong>Artifact stratum, per ecosystem.</strong>
npm: of {{ by_ecosystem.npm.n_examined }} packages examined,
{{ by_ecosystem.npm.aggregate.supports }} of {{ by_ecosystem.npm.aggregate.n }} show
published-artifact evidence of support for <span class="mono">{{ revision }}</span>
({{ by_ecosystem.npm.aggregate.does_not_support }} show no such evidence,
{{ by_ecosystem.npm.aggregate.unknown }} unknown) — {{ share_ci(by_ecosystem.npm.aggregate) }}.
PyPI: of {{ by_ecosystem.pypi.n_examined }} packages examined,
{{ by_ecosystem.pypi.aggregate.supports }} of {{ by_ecosystem.pypi.aggregate.n }} show such
evidence ({{ by_ecosystem.pypi.aggregate.does_not_support }} show no such evidence,
{{ by_ecosystem.pypi.aggregate.unknown }} unknown) — {{ share_ci(by_ecosystem.pypi.aggregate) }}.
<em>Pooled across both ecosystems, for reference only</em> — the registry's npm:PyPI split
means this figure does not describe either ecosystem: of {{ artifact_n_examined }} examined,
{{ artifact_agg.supports }} of {{ artifact_agg.n }} ({{ artifact_agg.unknown }} unknown) —
{{ share_ci(artifact_agg) }}.</p>

{% if probe_agg is none %}
<p><strong>Live-discover stratum.</strong> Not run. This project does not send unauthorised
active probes to third-party servers it has no relationship with; the live-discover stratum
this section could report requires exactly that, so no figure is stated here. This report does
not estimate live, ecosystem-wide support from artifact evidence alone.</p>
{% else %}
<p><strong>Live-discover stratum.</strong> Of a random sample of {{ probe_n }} remote MCP
servers, {{ probe_agg.supports }} answered a live discovery request in a way consistent with
support for <span class="mono">{{ revision }}</span>; {{ probe_agg.unknown }} unknown (no
answer, or excluded before a request was sent). A single unauthenticated probe can confirm
support; it can never confirm its absence, so this stratum does not report a does-not-support
count.</p>
{% endif %}

<p>These are two different populations, measured by two different methods. Neither figure is
combined with the other, and neither stands in for "the MCP ecosystem" as a whole.</p>
</div>

<h2>Collection window and sample</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Started</th><td class="mono">{{ run.started_at.isoformat() }}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Finished</th><td class="mono">{{ run.finished_at.isoformat() if run.finished_at else "in progress" }}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Population</th><td class="num" data-testid="population-size">{{ run.population_size }}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Sample seed</th><td class="num" data-testid="sample-seed">{{ run.sample_seed }}</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>Population by distribution</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Distribution</th><th class="num">Entries</th></tr>
{% for name, count in distribution.items() %}
<tr><td class="mono">{{ name }}</td><td class="num" data-testid="distribution-{{ name }}">{{ count }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table>
<p class="deriv"><strong>Scope.</strong> Tier 2 samples only from the
<span data-testid="eligible-count">{{ eligible_count }}</span> registry entries
with npm or PyPI package coordinates (<span class="mono">package_npm</span> and
<span class="mono">package_pypi</span> are fetchable). The
<span data-testid="package-other-count">{{ package_other_count }}</span>
<span class="mono">package_other</span> entries name an ecosystem this census does not model
and are not eligible. The {{ remote_only_count }} remote-only entries carry no fetchable
artifact and are unexamined by construction — every artifact-stratum figure below is a
statement about npm and PyPI packaged entries, never about the population as a whole.</p>

<h3>Fetch failures</h3>
<p data-testid="fetch-failures">Fetch failures: {{ run.fetch_failures }}
(<span data-testid="fetch-failures-registry">{{ fetch_failures.registry_pagination }}</span>
registry pagination,
<span data-testid="fetch-failures-artifact">{{ fetch_failures.artifact }}</span> artifact
fetch). A failed artifact fetch is excluded from every examined count and every denominator,
and is listed here as part of the sample, never as an unknown.</p>
{% if fetch_failures.by_cause %}
<table>
<tr><th>Artifact-fetch failure cause</th><th class="num">Count</th></tr>
{% for cause, count in fetch_failures.by_cause.items() %}
<tr><td>{{ cause }}</td><td class="num">{{ count }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table>
{% endif %}
{% if fetch_failures.by_ecosystem_status %}
<table>
<tr><th>Ecosystem</th><th>Fetch status</th><th class="num">Count</th></tr>
{% for eco, statuses in fetch_failures.by_ecosystem_status.items() %}
{% for status, count in statuses.items() %}
<tr><td class="mono">{{ eco }}</td><td class="mono">{{ status }}</td><td class="num">{{ count }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
</table>
{% endif %}

<h2>Artifact stratum</h2>
<p><strong>Method.</strong> {{ selection_method|safe }}</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Ecosystem</th><th class="num">Tier-2 target n</th><th class="num">Examined</th>
    <th class="num">Supports</th><th class="num">Does not support</th><th class="num">Unknown</th>
    <th class="num">Share</th></tr>
{% for eco, row in by_ecosystem.items() %}
<tr>
  <td class="mono">{{ eco }}</td>
  <td class="num">{{ run.tier2_n }}</td>
  <td class="num">{{ row.n_examined }}</td>
  <td class="num">{{ row.aggregate.supports }}</td>
  <td class="num">{{ row.aggregate.does_not_support }}</td>
  <td class="num">{{ row.aggregate.unknown }} unknown</td>
  <td class="num">{{ share_ci(row.aggregate) }}</td>
</tr>
{% endfor %}
<tr>
  <td class="mono"><strong>pooled (both ecosystems)</strong></td>
  <td class="num">—</td>
  <td class="num">{{ artifact_n_examined }}</td>
  <td class="num">{{ artifact_agg.supports }}</td>
  <td class="num">{{ artifact_agg.does_not_support }}</td>
  <td class="num">{{ artifact_agg.unknown }} unknown</td>
  <td class="num">{{ share_ci(artifact_agg) }}</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p class="deriv">Share is supports over n (unknowns excluded), with a Wilson score 95%
confidence interval — a statement about the seeded random sample's precision within its
ecosystem, not about deployments.</p>
<p class="deriv">Tier-2 target n is per ecosystem, not pooled: up to
<span data-testid="tier2-n">{{ run.tier2_n }}</span> npm packages and up to {{ run.tier2_n }}
PyPI packages are independently drawn at random (seed {{ run.sample_seed }}) within each
ecosystem before any artifact is fetched. The pooled row is for reference only.</p>

<h3>Detection limitations</h3>
<p class="deriv">"Supports" requires two signals in the published artifact: an SDK pin at or
above <span class="mono">{{ support_floor }}</span> <em>and</em> a
<span class="mono">server/discover</span> handler string in shipped source. Two known
under-counts follow from that rule; both are limitations of the method, not findings about
the packages concerned.</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Limitation</th><th class="num">npm</th><th class="num">PyPI</th><th class="num">Total</th></tr>
<tr>
  <td>Pinned at or above the floor, but no handler string in shipped source — counted as
  does not support. If the SDK serves <span class="mono">server/discover</span> on the
  package's behalf, each is a false does-not-support the artifact alone cannot resolve.</td>
  <td class="num" data-testid="pinned-without-handler-npm">{{ limitations.pinned_at_floor_without_handler.npm }}</td>
  <td class="num" data-testid="pinned-without-handler-pypi">{{ limitations.pinned_at_floor_without_handler.pypi }}</td>
  <td class="num" data-testid="pinned-without-handler-total">{{ limitations.pinned_at_floor_without_handler.total }}</td>
</tr>
<tr>
  <td>Source mentions a <span class="mono">{{ revision }}</span> feature, but the SDK pin
  predates the floor — the pin wins and the record counts as does not support.</td>
  <td class="num" data-testid="floor-dropped-npm">{{ limitations.floor_dropped_source_signal.npm }}</td>
  <td class="num" data-testid="floor-dropped-pypi">{{ limitations.floor_dropped_source_signal.pypi }}</td>
  <td class="num" data-testid="floor-dropped-total">{{ limitations.floor_dropped_source_signal.total }}</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p class="deriv">Both bias the reported share downward. "Supports {{ revision }}" is a
statement about a published artifact, not about any deployment's observed behaviour.</p>

<h2>Live-discover stratum</h2>
{% if probe_agg is none %}
<p>Not run. This project does not send unauthorised active probes to third-party servers it
has no relationship with, so no live-discover records exist in this publication.</p>
{% else %}
<table>
<tr><th class="num">Sampled</th><th class="num">Supports</th><th class="num">Unknown</th></tr>
<tr>
  <td class="num">{{ probe_n }}</td>
  <td class="num">{{ probe_agg.supports }}</td>
  <td class="num">{{ probe_agg.unknown }} unknown</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p class="deriv">No share/percentage is reported for this stratum. "Does not support" is
structurally always 0 here — a single probe can confirm support, never its absence (see
"live-discover sample" below) — so a supports-over-n ratio would look fully positive even when
most of the sample never answered at all. {{ probe_agg.unknown }} of the {{ probe_n }} sampled
hosts never answered a request, or were excluded before one was sent: that non-response count
is the number that matters here, not a derived percentage.</p>
{% endif %}

<h2>Terms</h2>
<dl data-testid="term-definitions">
{% for term, definition in term_definitions.items() %}
<dt><strong>{{ term }}</strong></dt>
<dd>{{ definition|safe }}</dd>
{% endfor %}
</dl>

<footer>
<h2>Methodology</h2>
<p>Tool version <span class="mono">{{ run.tool_version }}</span>, method hash
<span class="mono">{{ run.method_hash }}</span>. A changed collection method cannot silently
reuse this label - see the changelog below.</p>
<p>Raw data (digest-keyed, no names or URLs): <a href="records.csv">records.csv</a>. Reproduce
every number above with <a href="../../../analysis/census_analysis.py">analysis/census_analysis.py records.csv</a> -
no database, no salt, no API key required.</p>
<p>Secrets or other sensitive findings from this collection are handled per the
<a href="../../security.md">disclosure policy</a>, never published here.</p>
<p>Results are versioned, never overwritten: see the
<a href="../CHANGELOG.md">census changelog</a>.</p>
</footer>
</body>
</html>
